>> that "P is an emergent phenomenon, A means that "I do not see how P is a
>> predictable possible consequence of the elements, interactions, and initial
>> conditions of system S".  In other words "emergence" is a sense of surprise
>> in an observer, not a mysterious propert of a system.  Science -- that is,
>> reductionism -- proceeds by examining things until one understand enough to
>> be no longer surprised.

